# 27. Visual and Interaction Principles

### 1. Context over navigation

Keep users in Timeline rather than sending them through multiple screens.

### 2. Progressive disclosure

Show essential information first and reveal additional detail only when requested.

### 3. One Timeline surface

Dates, time periods, sessions, summaries, and application history should feel like different states of the same product surface.

### 4. Draggable depth

The Session Detail bottom sheet provides the first level of detail. Dragging it upward reveals the complete Application Timeline.

### 5. Quiet observation

The UI should document activity without judging it.

### 6. Visual evidence

Where platform capabilities allow it, screenshots should make activity more tangible.

### 7. Minimal architecture

The product should remain centered around one primary experience and one configuration screen.

### 8. Platform honesty

Android and iOS should expose the capabilities their respective platforms actually support rather than pretending they are technically identical.

### 9. Mechanical foundation

Tracking and session history must remain valuable independently of AI, analytics, or future intelligence.

